---
import DocLayout from "../../components/docs/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Configuration (.npkillrc)"
  description="Learn how to configure npkill with a .npkillrc file for custom defaults, profiles, and more."
>
  <h1>Configuration (.npkillrc)</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The <code>.npkillrc</code> file lets you configure npkill's default behavior,
    create custom profiles, and save your preferences so you don't have to specify
    them every time.
  </p>

  <h2>File Location</h2>
  <p>
    npkill looks for the configuration file in this order and uses the first one
    it finds:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li>The path given with the <code>--config</code> flag</li>
    <li><code>./.npkillrc</code> in the current directory</li>
    <li><code>~/.npkillrc</code> in your home directory</li>
  </ol>

  <CodeBlock code="npx npkill --config /path/to/my-config.json" />

  <h2>Configuration Options</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>.npkillrc</code> file uses JSON format. Here's a complete example:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "rootDir": "/home/user/projects",
  "exclude": ["important-project", "production-app"],
  "sortBy": "size",
  "sizeUnit": "auto",
  "excludeSensitiveResults": true,
  "dryRun": false,
  "defaultProfiles": ["node", "webdev"],
  "profiles": {
    "webdev": {
      "description": "Frontend artifacts and build outputs",
      "targets": ["dist", ".next", ".nuxt", ".output", "build"]
    }
  }
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Available Options</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Option</th>
          <th>Type</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>rootDir</code></td>
          <td>string</td>
          <td
            >Absolute path to start searching from. <code>~</code> is not expanded</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>exclude</code></td>
          <td>string[]</td>
          <td
            >Directories to skip, with the same patterns as <code>-E</code>.
            They are added to the ones given with <code>-E</code></td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>sortBy</code></td>
          <td>string</td>
          <td
            >Default sort order: "none", "size", "path" or "age". Default "none"</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>sizeUnit</code></td>
          <td>string</td>
          <td>Size display unit: "auto", "mb" or "gb". Default "auto"</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>excludeSensitiveResults</code></td>
          <td>boolean</td>
          <td>Whether to hide sensitive results. Default false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dryRun</code></td>
          <td>boolean</td>
          <td>Simulate deletions without deleting anything. Default false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>defaultProfiles</code></td>
          <td>string[]</td>
          <td
            >Profiles to use when you don't pass <code>-p</code> or <code
              >-t</code
            >. Built-in or your own, never empty. Default ["node"]</td
          >
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>profiles</code></td>
          <td>object</td>
          <td>Custom profile definitions</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Custom Profiles</h2>
  <p>
    You can define your own profiles in the <code>profiles</code> section. Each profile
    needs a name, description, and list of targets. A target is a folder name or
    a <a href="/docs/profiles#custom-rules">rule</a>:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "profiles": {
    "mystack": {
      "description": "My full-stack development artifacts",
      "targets": [
        "node_modules",
        "dist",
        ".next",
        "__pycache__",
        ".venv",
        "target"
      ]
    }
  }
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <p>Then use it with:</p>

  <CodeBlock code="npx npkill -p mystack" />

  <div class="warning">
    <i class="bx bx-error"></i>
    <div>
      Custom profiles with the same name as built-in profiles will override
      them. <code>all</code> is reserved.
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Priority Order</h2>
  <p>
    Options are applied in this order (later options override earlier ones):
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>.npkillrc file</strong> — Default configuration</li>
    <li><strong>CLI flags</strong> — Command-line arguments</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Options panel</strong> — Changes made in the TUI options panel (temporary)
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    This means you can set sensible defaults in your <code>.npkillrc</code> and override
    them when needed with CLI flags.
  </p>

  <h2>Example Configurations</h2>

  <h3>JavaScript Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "defaultProfiles": ["node"],
  "rootDir": "/home/user/dev",
  "sortBy": "size"
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Full-Stack Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "sortBy": "size",
  "defaultProfiles": ["node", "python"]
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h3>Game Developer</h3>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "rootDir": "/home/user/GameProjects",
  "defaultProfiles": ["unity", "unreal", "godot"]
}`}
    lang="json"
    filename="~/.npkillrc"
  />

  <h2>Validation</h2>
  <p>
    npkill checks the file every time it starts: unknown properties, types and
    values. If something is wrong, it shows a configuration error with the
    reason and exits without scanning. A missing <code>~/.npkillrc</code> is fine,
    but a file passed with <code>--config</code> must exist.
  </p>
</DocLayout>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .warning {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.3);
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .warning i {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-warning);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
</style>
